The Position

The mission of the Patient Care Country Expert is to deliver a seamless, positive experience for customers across multiple communication channels. Dedicated to efficiently resolving service requests and incidents, the Patient Care Advisor ensures proper classification, assignment, tracking, documentation, and follow-up to guarantee a satisfactory resolution.

By driving customer satisfaction through key performance indicators, the Patient Care Country Expert supports the leader with the internal and external teams to offer robust technical and medical support, manages adverse events and product complaints with high-quality customer service, and adheres to organizational, client, and regulatory guidelines. Committed to continuous development through necessary training, tools, and resources, the Patient Care Country Expert consistently delivers value to the team while operating with a global perspective and leveraging best practices.

The Patient Care Country Expert is reporting to the Customer Care Team Manager or other Customer Care Leader and is responsible for the technical, analytical and operational support of the area and coordinating country related topics. She/He could assist the leader in people management daily tasks and take over deputy functions in case of leader absence. Additionally is providing excellent customer front-line assistance through a variety of channels and technology to patients and customers related to Products and Digital Solutions commercialized by Roche, understanding their needs and following all the systems and procedures established.

Key Accountabilities:

• Leadership and Team Support

• Provide constructive feedback and coaching on technical and behavioral issues in partnership with the advisor’s leader or Supplier Operations Manager;

• Inspire and motivate the team by leading by example;

• Support leaders in quality-related topics and audit preparation;

• Assist in the recruitment process, including interviewing and initial candidate selection with People & Culture (P&C);

• Proactively support leaders in specific country-related topics, including country meetings, operational process implementation, and task distribution among advisors;

• In the leader’s absence, ensure the efficient running of daily operations;

• Communicate operational topics to the team and provide necessary follow-ups;

• Manage administrative team tasks such as holiday requests and absences.

• Country-Specific Expertise

• Act as the first point of contact for country-specific questions, escalating requests to leaders when necessary;

• Monitor and analyze KPIs, ensuring country procedures are correctly applied and identifying training needs;

• Provide training on country-specific topics and procedures to new advisors, and offer refresh training as needed;

• Maintain and update the knowledge base on country-related topics, informing advisors accordingly;

• Take ownership of adapting global processes to local markets by staying up-to-date with changing regulations and legal frameworks;

• Proactively propose improvements to existing workflows based on country-specific knowledge and insights.

• Customer Interaction and Support

• Handle escalated customer interactions and provide exemplary solutions;

• Address complex technical and marketing-oriented customer requests via phone and in writing;

• Process complaints in alignment with internal quality guidelines and regulatory provisions;

• Work with inbound workflow objects and manage custome

descriptionByLocale.it:
A Roche puoi apparire come te stesso, abbracciato per le qualità uniche che porti. La nostra cultura incoraggia l'espressione personale, il dialogo aperto e i legami genuini, dove siete valorizzati, accettati e rispettati per chi siete, permettendovi di prosperare sia personalmente che professionalmente. Questo è il modo in cui vogliamo prevenire, fermare e curare le malattie e garantire che tutti abbiano accesso alla salute oggi e per le generazioni a venire. Unisciti a Roche, dove ogni voce conta. La posizione La missione dell'esperto del paese di cura del paziente è quella di offrire un'esperienza senza soluzione di continuità e positiva per i clienti attraverso più canali di comunicazione. Dedicato a risolvere in modo efficiente le richieste e gli incidenti dei servizi, il Consulente di Assistenza Paziente garantisce una corretta classificazione, assegnazione, tracciamento, documentazione e follow-up per garantire una risoluzione soddisfacente. Guidando la soddisfazione del cliente attraverso i principali indicatori di performance, il paziente Care Country Expert supporta il leader con i team interni ed esterni per offrire un supporto tecnico e medico robusto, gestisce eventi avversi e reclami di prodotto con un servizio clienti di alta qualità e aderisce alle linee guida organizzative, client e normative. Impegnato allo sviluppo continuo attraverso la formazione, gli strumenti e le risorse necessarie, l'esperto del paese di cura del paziente fornisce costantemente valore al team, operando con una prospettiva globale e sfruttando le migliori pratiche. L'esperto per la cura del paziente sta segnalando al responsabile del team di assistenza clienti o altro responsabile dell'assistenza clienti ed è responsabile del supporto tecnico, analitico e operativo dell'area e del coordinamento degli argomenti relativi al paese. Poteva aiutare il leader nella gestione delle persone compiti quotidiani e assumere funzioni vice in caso di assenza leader. Inoltre sta fornendo un'eccellente assistenza clienti in prima linea attraverso una varietà di canali e tecnologie a pazienti e clienti relativi a Prodotti e Soluzioni Digitali commercializzati da Roche, comprendendo le loro esigenze e seguendo tutti i sistemi e le procedure stabilite. Capacità di contabilità chiave:
• Leadership e Team Support
• Fornire feedback costruttivi e coaching su problemi tecnici e comportamentali in collaborazione con il leader del consulente o Fornitore Operazioni Manager;
• Ispirare e motivare il team guidando per esempio;
• Sostenere i leader in materia di qualità e preparazione di audit;
• Assistere nel processo di reclutamento, compresa l'intervista e la selezione iniziale dei candidati con People & Culture (P&C);
• Sostenere attivamente i leader in specifici argomenti relativi al paese, tra cui riunioni di paese, implementazione dei processi operativi e distribuzione dei compiti tra i consulenti;
• In assenza del leader, garantire l'efficiente funzionamento delle operazioni quotidiane;
• Comunicare argomenti operativi al team e fornire i necessari follow-up;
• Gestisci i compiti del team amministrativo come richieste di vacanza e assenze.
• Competenza Paese-Specifico
• Agire come primo punto di contatto per le domande specifiche del paese, aumentando le richieste ai leader quando necessario;
• Monitorare e analizzare i KPI, assicurando che le procedure di campagna siano correttamente applicate e identificare le esigenze di formazione;
• Fornire formazione su argomenti e procedure specifiche del paese a nuovi consulenti, e offrire formazione di aggiornamento secondo le necessità;
• Mantenere e aggiornare la base di conoscenza su argomenti relativi al paese, informare i consulenti di conseguenza;
• Assumere la proprietà di adattare i processi globali ai mercati locali rimanendo aggiornati con cambiamenti di regolamenti e quadri legali;
• Propondere attivamente miglioramenti ai flussi di lavoro esistenti basati su conoscenze e approfondimenti specifici per il paese.
• Interazione del cliente e supporto
• Mantenere le interazioni dei clienti escalate e fornire soluzioni esemplari;
• Rivolgersi a complesse richieste tecniche e orientate al marketing tramite telefono e per iscritto;
• Denunce di processo in allineamento con le linee guida di qualità interna e le disposizioni regolamentari;
• Lavorare con oggetti a flusso di lavoro in entrata e gestire personalizzati

descriptionByLocale.en:
At Roche you can show up as yourself, embraced for the unique qualities you bring. Our culture encourages personal expression, open dialogue, and genuine connections, where you are valued, accepted and respected for who you are, allowing you to thrive both personally and professionally. This is how we aim to prevent, stop and cure diseases and ensure everyone has access to healthcare today and for generations to come. Join Roche, where every voice matters.

The Position

The mission of the Patient Care Country Expert is to deliver a seamless, positive experience for customers across multiple communication channels. Dedicated to efficiently resolving service requests and incidents, the Patient Care Advisor ensures proper classification, assignment, tracking, documentation, and follow-up to guarantee a satisfactory resolution.

By driving customer satisfaction through key performance indicators, the Patient Care Country Expert supports the leader with the internal and external teams to offer robust technical and medical support, manages adverse events and product complaints with high-quality customer service, and adheres to organizational, client, and regulatory guidelines. Committed to continuous development through necessary training, tools, and resources, the Patient Care Country Expert consistently delivers value to the team while operating with a global perspective and leveraging best practices.

The Patient Care Country Expert is reporting to the Customer Care Team Manager or other Customer Care Leader and is responsible for the technical, analytical and operational support of the area and coordinating country related topics. She/He could assist the leader in people management daily tasks and take over deputy functions in case of leader absence. Additionally is providing excellent customer front-line assistance through a variety of channels and technology to patients and customers related to Products and Digital Solutions commercialized by Roche, understanding their needs and following all the systems and procedures established.

Key Accountabilities:

• Leadership and Team Support

• Provide constructive feedback and coaching on technical and behavioral issues in partnership with the advisor’s leader or Supplier Operations Manager;

• Inspire and motivate the team by leading by example;

• Support leaders in quality-related topics and audit preparation;

• Assist in the recruitment process, including interviewing and initial candidate selection with People & Culture (P&C);

• Proactively support leaders in specific country-related topics, including country meetings, operational process implementation, and task distribution among advisors;

• In the leader’s absence, ensure the efficient running of daily operations;

• Communicate operational topics to the team and provide necessary follow-ups;

• Manage administrative team tasks such as holiday requests and absences.

• Country-Specific Expertise

• Act as the first point of contact for country-specific questions, escalating requests to leaders when necessary;

• Monitor and analyze KPIs, ensuring country procedures are correctly applied and identifying training needs;

• Provide training on country-specific topics and procedures to new advisors, and offer refresh training as needed;

• Maintain and update the knowledge base on country-related topics, informing advisors accordingly;

• Take ownership of adapting global processes to local markets by staying up-to-date with changing regulations and legal frameworks;

• Proactively propose improvements to existing workflows based on country-specific knowledge and insights.

• Customer Interaction and Support

• Handle escalated customer interactions and provide exemplary solutions;

• Address complex technical and marketing-oriented customer requests via phone and in writing;

• Process complaints in alignment with internal quality guidelines and regulatory provisions;

• Work with inbound workflow objects and manage custome

descriptionByLocale.de:
Bei Roche können Sie sich als Sie selbst zeigen, umarmt für die einzigartigen Qualitäten, die Sie mitbringen. Unsere Kultur fördert persönlichen Ausdruck, offenen Dialog und echte Verbindungen, in denen Sie geschätzt, akzeptiert und respektiert werden, wer Sie sind, so dass Sie sowohl persönlich als auch beruflich gedeihen können. Auf diese Weise wollen wir Krankheiten verhindern, stoppen und heilen und sicherstellen, dass jeder heute und für kommende Generationen Zugang zu Gesundheitsversorgung hat. Treten Sie Roche bei, wo jede Stimme wichtig ist. Die Position Die Mission des Patient Care Country Expert ist es, Kunden über mehrere Kommunikationskanäle hinweg eine nahtlose, positive Erfahrung zu bieten. Der Patient Care Advisor, der sich der effizienten Lösung von Serviceanfragen und Vorfällen widmet, sorgt für eine ordnungsgemäße Klassifizierung, Zuordnung, Nachverfolgung, Dokumentation und Nachverfolgung, um eine zufriedenstellende Lösung zu gewährleisten. Durch die Steigerung der Kundenzufriedenheit durch wichtige Leistungsindikatoren unterstützt der Patient Care Country Expert die Führungskraft mit den internen und externen Teams, um robuste technische und medizinische Unterstützung anzubieten, unerwünschte Ereignisse und Produktbeschwerden mit hochwertigem Kundenservice zu bewältigen und sich an organisatorische, kundenbezogene und regulatorische Richtlinien zu halten. Der Patient Care Country Expert, der sich der kontinuierlichen Entwicklung durch notwendige Schulungen, Tools und Ressourcen verschrieben hat, liefert dem Team konsequent Wert, während er mit einer globalen Perspektive arbeitet und Best Practices nutzt. Der Patient Care Country Expert berichtet dem Customer Care Team Manager oder einem anderen Customer Care Leader und ist für die technische, analytische und operative Unterstützung des Bereichs und die Koordination länderbezogener Themen verantwortlich. Sie / Er könnte den Leiter bei der Verwaltung täglicher Aufgaben unterstützen und im Falle einer Abwesenheit des Leiters stellvertretende Funktionen übernehmen. Darüber hinaus bietet es Patienten und Kunden im Zusammenhang mit Produkten und digitalen Lösungen, die von Roche kommerzialisiert werden, hervorragende Unterstützung an vorderster Front durch eine Vielzahl von Kanälen und Technologien, um ihre Bedürfnisse zu verstehen und alle etablierten Systeme und Verfahren zu befolgen. Hauptverantwortlichkeiten:
• Führung und Team Support
• konstruktives Feedback und Coaching zu technischen und Verhaltensfragen in Zusammenarbeit mit dem Leiter des Beraters oder dem Supplier Operations Manager;
• Inspirieren und motivieren Sie das Team, indem Sie mit gutem Beispiel vorangehen;
• Unterstützung von Führungskräften bei qualitätsbezogenen Themen und der Vorbereitung von Audits;
• Unterstützung beim Rekrutierungsprozess, einschließlich Interviews und anfänglicher Kandidatenauswahl mit People & Culture (P&C);
• Proaktive Unterstützung von Führungskräften bei spezifischen länderbezogenen Themen, einschließlich Ländertreffen, Implementierung von operativen Prozessen und Aufgabenverteilung unter Beratern;
• In Abwesenheit des Leiters die effiziente Durchführung des täglichen Betriebs sicherstellen;
• Kommunizieren Sie operative Themen an das Team und sorgen Sie für notwendige Folgemaßnahmen;
• Verwalten Sie administrative Teamaufgaben wie Urlaubsanfragen und Abwesenheiten.
• Länderspezifische Expertise
• Als erster Ansprechpartner für länderspezifische Fragen fungieren und bei Bedarf Anfragen an Führungskräfte eskalieren lassen;
• Überwachung und Analyse der KPIs, Gewährleistung der korrekten Anwendung der Verfahren in den Ländern und Ermittlung des Schulungsbedarfs;
• Bereitstellung von Schulungen zu länderspezifischen Themen und Verfahren für neue Berater und gegebenenfalls Bereitstellung von Auffrischungsschulungen;
• Pflegen und aktualisieren Sie die Wissensbasis zu länderbezogenen Themen und informieren Sie die Berater entsprechend;
• Übernahme der Verantwortung für die Anpassung globaler Prozesse an lokale Märkte, indem Sie mit sich ändernden Vorschriften und rechtlichen Rahmenbedingungen auf dem Laufenden bleiben;
• Proaktive Verbesserung bestehender Workflows basierend auf länderspezifischem Wissen und Erkenntnissen.
• Kundeninteraktion und Support
• Umgang mit eskalierten Kundeninteraktionen und Bereitstellung beispielhafter Lösungen;
• Adressieren Sie komplexe technische und marketingorientierte Kundenanfragen telefonisch und schriftlich;
• Bearbeitung von Beschwerden in Übereinstimmung mit internen Qualitätsrichtlinien und regulatorischen Bestimmungen;
• Arbeiten mit Inbound Workflow-Objekten und Verwalten von Custome

descriptionByLocale.fr:
Chez Roche vous pouvez vous montrer comme vous-même, embrassé pour les qualités uniques que vous apportez. Notre culture encourage l'expression personnelle, le dialogue ouvert et les liens authentiques, où vous êtes apprécié, accepté et respecté pour qui vous êtes, vous permettant de prospérer à la fois personnellement et professionnellement. C'est ainsi que nous visons à prévenir, à arrêter et à guérir les maladies et à veiller à ce que chacun ait accès aux soins de santé aujourd'hui et pour les générations à venir. Rejoignez Roche, où chaque voix compte. La position La mission du Patient Care Country Expert est de fournir une expérience positive et transparente aux clients sur plusieurs canaux de communication. Destiné à résoudre efficacement les demandes de services et les incidents, le conseiller en soins aux patients assure la classification, l'affectation, le suivi, la documentation et le suivi appropriés pour garantir une résolution satisfaisante. En favorisant la satisfaction de la clientèle grâce à des indicateurs de performance clés, l'expert en soins aux patients accompagne le chef de file auprès des équipes internes et externes afin d'offrir un soutien technique et médical solide, de gérer les événements indésirables et les plaintes de produits avec un service à la clientèle de haute qualité et de respecter les lignes directrices organisationnelles, clientes et réglementaires. Engagé dans le développement continu grâce à la formation, aux outils et aux ressources nécessaires, le Patient Care Country Expert offre systématiquement de la valeur à l'équipe tout en travaillant dans une perspective mondiale et en tirant parti des meilleures pratiques. L'expert en soins aux patients relève du gestionnaire de l'équipe de soins aux clients ou d'un autre responsable des soins aux clients et est responsable de l'appui technique, analytique et opérationnel du domaine et de la coordination des sujets liés au pays. Il/elle pourrait aider le chef dans les tâches quotidiennes de gestion des personnes et prendre la relève en cas d'absence de chef. De plus, elle fournit une excellente assistance en première ligne à ses clients par l'entremise de divers canaux et technologies aux patients et clients liés aux produits et solutions numériques commercialisés par Roche, en comprenant leurs besoins et en suivant tous les systèmes et procédures établis. Responsabilités clés :
• Leadership et appui aux équipes
• Fournir des commentaires constructifs et un encadrement sur les questions techniques et comportementales en partenariat avec le chef du conseiller ou le gestionnaire des opérations du fournisseur;
• Inspirer et motiver l'équipe en donnant l'exemple;
• soutenir les dirigeants dans les domaines liés à la qualité et la préparation des audits;
• Aider au processus de recrutement, y compris l'entrevue et la sélection initiale des candidats auprès de People & Culture (P&C);
• d) Aider activement les dirigeants à traiter de sujets spécifiques concernant les pays, notamment les réunions de pays, la mise en œuvre des processus opérationnels et la répartition des tâches entre les conseillers;
• En l'absence du leader, assurer le fonctionnement efficace des opérations quotidiennes;
• Communiquer les sujets opérationnels à l'équipe et fournir les suivis nécessaires;
• Gérer les tâches de l'équipe administrative comme les demandes de vacances et les absences.
• Expertise par pays
• Agir en tant que premier point de contact pour les questions spécifiques à chaque pays, en intensifiant les demandes aux dirigeants si nécessaire;
• Surveiller et analyser les ICR, veiller à ce que les procédures nationales soient correctement appliquées et déterminer les besoins de formation;
• Dispenser une formation sur des sujets et des procédures propres à chaque pays aux nouveaux conseillers et offrir une formation de recyclage au besoin;
• Maintenir et mettre à jour la base de connaissances sur les sujets liés aux pays, en informant les conseillers en conséquence;
• S'approprier l'adaptation des processus mondiaux aux marchés locaux en se tenant au courant de l'évolution des réglementations et des cadres juridiques;
• Proposer activement des améliorations aux flux de travail existants en se fondant sur les connaissances et les connaissances propres à chaque pays.
• Interaction client et soutien
• gérer les interactions avec les clients et fournir des solutions exemplaires;
• Répondre aux demandes complexes des clients sur les plans technique et marketing par téléphone et par écrit;
• traiter les plaintes conformément aux lignes directrices internes sur la qualité et aux dispositions réglementaires;
• Travailler avec les objets de workflow entrants et gérer personnalisé

jobs.description:
At Roche you can show up as yourself, embraced for the unique qualities you bring. Our culture encourages personal expression, open dialogue, and genuine connections, where you are valued, accepted and respected for who you are, allowing you to thrive both personally and professionally. This is how we aim to prevent, stop and cure diseases and ensure everyone has access to healthcare today and for generations to come. Join Roche, where every voice matters.

The Position
Como Especialista de Custos e Eficiência em Supply Chain, você será o agente de transformação da nossa operação. Seu papel une o conhecimento das operações de Transportes e Armazenagem à governança financeira dos custos logísticos, com foco em ganho de eficiência e acuracidade do P&L da companhia.

Sobre a oportunidade:

• Gestão de Custos e Performance: Analisar e gerir os custos logísticos (P&L), identificando oportunidades de economia, ganhos de eficiência operacional e gestão das provisões.

• Analisar mensalmente em conjunto com a área de operações, as faturas enviadas pelos fornecedores, verificando a acuracidade dos valores envolvidos, além de confrontar tais valores versus orçamento previsto, atuando a minimizar os desvios encontrados e correções de rotas necessárias;

• Apoiar a construção do plano orçamentário de curto e médio prazo dos gastos logísticos, bem como dos projetos estratégicos da diretoria com foco em melhoria de performance e alcance de eficiências operacionais/financeiras;

• Controlar os custos de frete (Inbound/Outbound), taxas de armazenagem, despachante, nacionalização, adequação, entre outros;

• Identificar gargalos operacionais que geram desperdícios e propor projetos de redução de custos (Saving);

• Monitorar impactos financeiros dos KPI’s operacionais quanto a performance dos principais fornecedores (armazenagem e transporte);

• Excelência Operacional: Mapear e redesenhar processos de ponta a ponta (Armazenagem e Transportes), implementando fluxos sustentáveis e documentação de treinamento;

• Interface Estratégica: Colaborar diretamente com a liderança de Supply Chain Excellence para desdobrar a estratégia global em ações locais.

Quem você é:

• Bacharelado em Administração, Economia, Engenharia de Produção, Ciências Contábeis, Logística ou áreas correlatas;

• Sólida experiência anterior na área de controladoria logística, custos logísticos ou planejamento financeiro de supply chain;

• Experiência em operações de Logística Outbound e Order Management;

• Experiência em ferramentas de melhoria contínua e gestão de projetos

• Excel Avançado (obrigatório para modelagem de dados).

• Domínio de ferramentas de BI (Power BI, Tableau) para criação de relatórios.

• Desejável conhecimento em SAP módulos SD e MM

• Familiaridade com conceitos fiscais e tributários ligados ao transporte (ICMS, ISS, crédito de PIS/COFINS).

• Fluência em Inglês e Português

• Forte capacidade analítica e atenção aos detalhes;

• Resiliência e forte habilidade de articulação cross- supply

• Disponibilidade para atuar com base na zona sul de São Paulo, modelo híbrido (3x escritório)

Os benefícios de realocação não estão disponíveis para essa posição.

Who we are
A healthier future drives us to innovate. Together, more than 100’000 employees across the globe are dedicated to advance science, ensuring everyone has access to healthcare today and for generations to come. Our efforts result in more than 26 million people treated with our medicines and over 30 billion tests conducted using our Diagnostics products. We empower each other to explore new possibilities, foster creativity, and keep our ambitions high, so we can deliver life-changing healthcare solutions that make a global impact.

Let’s build a healthier future, together.

Roche is an Equal Opportunity Employer.

